{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "bookCode": "RV10",
  "bookSlug": "rig-veda-book-10",
  "n": 135,
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "refId": "RV10-135:1",
      "text": "translated by"
    },
    {
      "n": 2,
      "refId": "RV10-135:2",
      "text": "1. IN the Tree clothed with goodly leaves where Yama drinketh with the Gods,",
      "original": "यस्मिन्वृक्षे सुपलाशे देवैः सम्पिबते यमः ।",
      "translit": "yasminvṛkṣe supalāśe devaiḥ sampibate yamaḥ |"
    },
    {
      "n": 3,
      "refId": "RV10-135:3",
      "text": "The Father, Master of the house, tendeth with love our ancient Sires.",
      "original": "अत्रा नो विश्पतिः पिता पुराणाँ अनु वेनति",
      "translit": "atrā no viśpatiḥ pitā purāṇām̐ anu venati"
    },
    {
      "n": 4,
      "refId": "RV10-135:4",
      "text": "2. I looked reluctantly on him who cherishes those men of old,",
      "original": "पुराणाँ अनुवेनन्तं चरन्तं पापयामुया ।",
      "translit": "purāṇām̐ anuvenantaṃ carantaṃ pāpayāmuyā |"
    },
    {
      "n": 5,
      "refId": "RV10-135:5",
      "text": "On him who treads that evil path, and then I yearned for this again.",
      "original": "असूयन्नभ्यचाकशं तस्मा अस्पृहयं पुनः",
      "translit": "asūyannabhyacākaśaṃ tasmā aspṛhayaṃ punaḥ"
    },
    {
      "n": 6,
      "refId": "RV10-135:6",
      "text": "3. Thou mountest, though thou dost not see, O Child, the new and wheel-less car",
      "original": "यं कुमार नवं रथमचक्रं मनसाकृणोः ।",
      "translit": "yaṃ kumāra navaṃ rathamacakraṃ manasākṛṇoḥ |"
    },
    {
      "n": 7,
      "refId": "RV10-135:7",
      "text": "Which thou hast fashioned mentally, one poled but turning every way.",
      "original": "एकेषं विश्वतः प्राञ्चमपश्यन्नधि तिष्ठसि",
      "translit": "ekeṣaṃ viśvataḥ prāñcamapaśyannadhi tiṣṭhasi"
    },
    {
      "n": 8,
      "refId": "RV10-135:8",
      "text": "4. The car which thou hast made to roll hitherward from the Sages, Child!",
      "original": "यं कुमार प्रावर्तयो रथं विप्रेभ्यस्परि ।",
      "translit": "yaṃ kumāra prāvartayo rathaṃ viprebhyaspari |"
    },
    {
      "n": 9,
      "refId": "RV10-135:9",
      "text": "This hath the Saman followed close, hence, laid together on a ship.",
      "original": "तं सामानु प्रावर्तत समितो नाव्याहितम्",
      "translit": "taṃ sāmānu prāvartata samito nāvyāhitam"
    },
    {
      "n": 10,
      "refId": "RV10-135:10",
      "text": "5. Who was the father of the child? Who made the chariot roll away?",
      "original": "कः कुमारमजनयद्रथं को निरवर्तयत् ।",
      "translit": "kaḥ kumāramajanayadrathaṃ ko niravartayat |"
    },
    {
      "n": 11,
      "refId": "RV10-135:11",
      "text": "Who will this day declare to us how the funeral gift was made?",
      "original": "कः स्वित्तदद्य नो ब्रूयादनुदेयी यथाभवत्",
      "translit": "kaḥ svittadadya no brūyādanudeyī yathābhavat"
    },
    {
      "n": 12,
      "refId": "RV10-135:12",
      "text": "6. When the funeral gift was placed, straightway the point of flame appeared.",
      "original": "यथाभवदनुदेयी ततो अग्रमजायत ।",
      "translit": "yathābhavadanudeyī tato agramajāyata |"
    },
    {
      "n": 13,
      "refId": "RV10-135:13",
      "text": "A depth extended in the front: a passage out was made behind.",
      "original": "पुरस्ताद्बुध्न आततः पश्चान्निरयणं कृतम्",
      "translit": "purastādbudhna ātataḥ paścānnirayaṇaṃ kṛtam"
    },
    {
      "n": 14,
      "refId": "RV10-135:14",
      "text": "7. Here is the seat where Yama dwells, that which is called the Home of Gods:",
      "original": "इदं यमस्य सादनं देवमानं यदुच्यते ।",
      "translit": "idaṃ yamasya sādanaṃ devamānaṃ yaducyate |"
    },
    {
      "n": 15,
      "refId": "RV10-135:15",
      "text": "Here minstrels blow the flute for him here he is glorified with songs.",
      "original": "इयमस्य धम्यते नाळीरयं गीर्भिः परिष्कृतः",
      "translit": "iyamasya dhamyate nāḷīrayaṃ gīrbhiḥ pariṣkṛtaḥ"
    }
  ]
}
